**Summary of All Findings**

All twelve checks in this batch resulted in findings of **not bug-bounty eligible**, with all three audit phases completing without identifying exploitable vulnerabilities. The following key security properties were verified:

**CHK-0116 (Proof Byte Length / Buffer Overflow):**
The SSZ decoder in `/target_workspace/proto/prysm/v1alpha1/fulu.ssz.go` at line 2107 uses `ssz.DivideInt2(len(buf), 48, 4096)` for both KzgCommitments and KzgProofs, and `DivideInt2(len(buf), 2048, 4096)` for Column. Any non-48-byte proof or non-2048-byte cell causes SSZ deserialization failure before any KZG code is reached.

**CHK-0117 (Array Length Consistency):**
Three independent enforcement layers exist: (1) SSZ enforces per-element byte sizes, (2) `VerifyDataColumnSidecar` at `/target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/peerdas/p2p_interface.go:47` checks `len(Column) == len(KzgCommitments) == len(KzgProofs)`, (3) the ckzg4844 Go binding at `/home/gohan/go/pkg/mod/github.com/ethereum/c-kzg-4844/v2@v2.1.1/bindings/go/main.go:508` checks all four array lengths are equal.

**CHK-0118 (Validation Layer Bypass):**
No bypass exists. The validation chain is sequential and each step gates the next. SSZ rejects bad byte lengths; `ValidFields` rejects count mismatches; ckzg4844 rejects remaining inconsistencies.

**CHK-0121, CHK-0122, CHK-0123, CHK-0124 (Subgroup Validation):**
The `validate_kzg_g1` function in `/home/gohan/go/pkg/mod/github.com/ethereum/c-kzg-4844/v2@v2.1.1/src/common/bytes.c:81-95` calls `blst_p1_in_g1` to enforce G1 subgroup membership for both commitments (via `bytes_to_kzg_commitment`) and proofs (via `bytes_to_kzg_proof`). This is called during `compute_weighted_sum_of_commitments` and the proof-to-G1 conversion loop inside `verify_cell_kzg_proof_batch`. Non-subgroup points return `C_KZG_BADARGS`, not a false positive. The blst library is the correct and production-grade implementation.

**CHK-0125, CHK-0126, CHK-0127, CHK-0128 (Commitment Deduplication):**
The `deduplicate_commitments` function at `/home/gohan/go/pkg/mod/github.com/ethereum/c-kzg-4844/v2@v2.1.1/src/eip7594/eip7594.c:343-374` correctly implements content-addressed deduplication using byte equality. The mapping invariant `deduplicated_commitments[commitment_indices[k]] == original_commitments_bytes[k]` holds by construction. No off-by-one exists. Weight accumulation in `compute_weighted_sum_of_commitments` at line 517-523 correctly aggregates weights per unique commitment. No attack exploiting commitment ordering is feasible because deduplication is purely content-addressed.

